AI-assisted: built with Codex

Related: #172837. Follow-up to #175246.

## What Problem This Solves

A parent request is refused as claimed by active work after a native Codex follow-up finishes while its result still awaits acknowledgment.

## User Impact

The parent can cold-resume to receive the completed result. Active child execution stays protected, and pending results and submission receipts remain available until acknowledgment.

## Why This Change Was Made

After successful follow-up admission, the existing monitor owns execution protection. Release the redundant submission-owned execution hold at that handoff; retain completion custody and receipt settlement under their existing owners. No schema, configuration, or delivery-policy change is needed.

Thanks to @linancn (Nan LI) for the fix and original proof. This builds on #175246’s terminal-parent retention repair.

## Evidence

- On main `397807c7374c41ffe434215e1e091edba2997474`, both acknowledgment-order regressions fail at `releaseCodexBoundLiveThread` with the terminal parent still claimed; the other 20 custody tests pass. With the fix, all 22 custody tests pass, including active-child protection, pending receipt preservation, and exactly-once consumption after acknowledgment. The 22 custody cases total 421ms of test execution; baseline wrapper time was 273.67s, dominated by preparation. The seven selected custody, retention, release-retry, delivery, submission-store, and runner suites pass: 90/90 tests across two shards, 901.05s wrapper time on this host. After integrating main `c8dfebcfaee8e8c25e9fee79304b59dd00717d8d`, the affected custody file passes again (22/22; 376.91s Vitest duration, dominated by worker preparation).
- Targeted extension oxlint and oxfmt pass. Independent Codex autoreview is scoped-clean with no P0–P2 findings. The broader changed-file runner passed production typechecking, plugin contract tests (10/10), and static guards. It caught a missing timing boolean in the new test; that is corrected and extension-test typechecking passes. Its precommit environment-budget comparison also passes after integration (457/457). Dead-export scans report 72 production, 1,136 script, and 84 full-tree entries, all in files unchanged from integrated main and none in this PR; no separate full base scan was run.
- Production delta: +2/-2 (net zero); test delta: +82/-27 (net +55). The regression uses the actual cold-resume guard in both predecessor-acknowledgment orders. Shared notification fixtures replace old notification literals; callback-level retention instrumentation was removed because the active-work guard covers the behavior directly.
- The prior real Codex 0.162.1 replay below drives native spawn and `send_input` with a scripted provider and held delivery acknowledgment: base rejects terminal parent resume, fixed execution protects active work then allows actual `thread/resume` with a pending receipt; acknowledgment consumes once. Its binding backend is in-memory, so it does not prove disk durability.
- The prior isolated authenticated Gateway smoke at `1cb15871a7f99b0f7af6346f2a04581344dd1928` returns `LIVE_A_OK`, `LIVE_B_OK`, and `LIVE_NEXT_OK`. No fresh authenticated Gateway/channel run was made here: the existing live lane requires provider credentials and does not inject the pending-acknowledgment interval; building a new harness exceeds the best-effort live budget.
- [Independent validation](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/177577#issuecomment-6354417596) separates this submission pin from the interrupted-child pin fixed by merged #179099. Open consolidation #174900 does not contain this submission-owner change.

This fixes the stated follow-up lockout. Broader delivery retry and abandonment policy in #172837 remains outside this Related-only PR.

