## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: when a model spends its whole output budget on reasoning (`max_tokens` / `length` with only a thinking block), OpenClaw sends a paid retry that says "Continue from that partial turn", but provider replay has already dropped that partial turn, so the model is asked to continue something it cannot see.

Related: #182178

## User Impact

A reasoning-only turn cut off at the output token limit now ends with the existing notice, "⚠️ The model reached its output token limit before generating an answer. Please try again.", instead of one or two extra paid requests that resend the same history plus an instruction about a missing turn. In the reported `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5` case those requests were refused as `reasoning_extraction`, and the user was told to revise a request OpenClaw had written.

Unchanged: reasoning-only turns that stop normally still get the visible-answer continuation, because replay keeps their signed thinking. Structured provider refusals stay terminal: no retry, no model fallback. Configured model fallbacks for incomplete `length` turns keep their existing behavior. No prompt, config, or schema changes.

## Why This Change Was Made

Two rules disagreed. #66167 added the reasoning-only continuation on the premise that the partial reasoning is replayed. #88656 later omitted reasoning-only `length` turns from replay for every provider, through `isReasoningOnlyLengthAssistantTurn` in both replay owners (embedded replay and the shared transport transform). Continuation eligibility now uses that same predicate, so OpenClaw only asks to continue a turn that replay actually sends. The check sits in the reasoning-only continuation owner, so it covers every route that uses it: Anthropic Messages, Anthropic-compatible providers, OpenAI Responses and Completions. OpenAI Responses `previous_response_id` continuation cannot carry the dropped turn either, because it requires the replayed history to contain the previous response output.

The issue's remaining risks:

- **Refusal trigger.** This PR does not change `REASONING_ONLY_RETRY_INSTRUCTION`. The third reported refusal followed a normal-stop turn whose signed thinking was replayed, so whether this wording trips Anthropic's classifier still needs a live A/B on `claude-opus-5-5`: the same history with and without the instruction. That stays open on #182178, hence `Related` rather than `Closes`.
- **Shared prompt and sibling providers.** Eligibility follows the provider-neutral replay rule rather than a provider allowlist, and the regression covers four routes for both stop reasons.
- **Accepted edge case.** If a normal-stop retry is followed by a `length` turn that also compacted mid-attempt, the existing compaction continuation still runs and keeps the earlier retry prompt alongside its own instruction. Base sends the same instruction in that sequence through the second reasoning-only retry, so this PR does not make it worse. Changing which internal prompt survives compaction belongs to the session prompt-state owner and is out of scope here.

## Evidence

**Regression test (red on base, green with the fix):** `continues $provider/$api reasoning only while replay keeps the turn` in `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/terminal-resolution.test.ts`. For `anthropic/anthropic-messages` (signed), `kimi/anthropic-messages` (unsigned), `openai/openai-responses` and `openai/openai-completions`, it asserts that `normalizeAssistantReplayContent` and `transformTransportMessages` keep the `stop` turn and drop the `length` turn, then runs `resolveEmbeddedRunTerminal`. On base, all four fail with `expected 'retry' to be 'complete'` on the `length` case while every `stop` control passes. With the fix, all four pass: `stop` still retries with the continuation, and `length` completes with the output-limit notice and `incomplete_turn` without activating any internal prompt.

**Isolated Gateway proof** (local harness, not committed; source below): a real Gateway (`startGatewayWithClient`, isolated temp state dir and port), the real `anthropic-messages` transport, and a loopback Anthropic Messages SSE server. Each scenario sends one `chat.send` and records every provider request: whether it carries the reasoning-only retry instruction, whether it carries the partial thinking signature, and what `chat.history` shows afterwards. Base is a checkout of `3bcc91708d8` with the production file unchanged; the fix run is this PR head `dae39368e86`. Both runs used `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.e2e.config.ts test/issue182178-reasoning-only-length.proof.e2e.test.ts` and exited 0 with `Tests 3 passed (3)`.

