Related: #114797

## What Problem This Solves

Changing watched groups or their titles rewrites the system suffix ahead of existing conversation history on generic OpenAI-compatible routes, breaking an otherwise reusable serialized request prefix.

## User Impact

Watched-group awareness stays current without rewriting earlier request context. Existing same-agent, main-session, read-tool, sandbox, and full-prompt gates remain in force; no read or send permission is added. No configuration or data migration is required.

## Why This Change Was Made

Keep the watch preparer's admitted snapshot beside its governed turn in the existing runtime carrier, including an explicit empty snapshot when the last readable watch disappears. Tool-context refresh accepts the refreshed snapshot without inserting it back into the system prompt. The released builder/SDK and separate compaction prompt keep their existing contracts; no new registry, cache, or persistence mechanism is introduced.

## Evidence

Reviewed/proven head: `5e06d92c71d5d8b44a67de0af4ec471adae90d26` (base `3bcc91708d8`). **83 focused tests across six files pass** (256.60 s serial wall); targeted format, oxlint, production core types, and owning nested-agent test types pass. The new real-storage regression took 5.177 s; CI seconds are pending, not estimated. Exact-head QA runtime build passed in 2m24s with `inputsClean: true`.

**Default Codex autoreview ran before commit/opening:** exit 0, validated `scoped-clean`, default **P0** threshold, complete single attempt, no accepted/actionable findings. It reviewed this candidate and supplied carrier/replay context; the subsequently recorded cold-process proof was not part of its input. No whole-repository or CI pass is claimed.

**Real transport after the fix:** four HTTP requests across two distinct source-Gateway processes pass. Empty → watch added → cold reopen/title renamed → final watch removed: all system/tool bytes and each prior request-message prefix remain identical. Current watch awareness reaches the new turn; original carrier bytes survive reopening; removal appends an explicit empty snapshot. Both Gateways shut down cleanly with agent-database clean-close receipts.

Production delta: three files +50/−12. The existing watch owner retains disclosure checks; the only new option requests its empty snapshot. No parallel policy or new durable schema. One composed +81-line owner regression covers the transition, refresh, revocation and excluded modes; existing watcher tests retain sorting/cap/sandbox/currentness coverage.

Verified baseline: pristine production main `3bcc91708d8ee794e52f9cb0ae98ebb1f848ad25`, Node 24.22.1. The real isolated source Gateway admitted two system tasks and awaited durable embedded turns against a loopback HTTP provider. Both returned the scripted final result. Adding one watch produced:

