The driver starts a stock source Gateway, validates its isolated config, authenticates a client, and runs admitted system tasks through the durable embedded runner. It uses the existing watch registration/title writers and a deterministic local HTTP provider; no module mocks, production state, real credentials or external sends.

Save this as `proof-row12-watched-context.mts` at the reviewed checkout root. The baseline used the same stock system-task/embedded flow; the final driver adds build/PID/hash receipts and explicit positive/removal assertions. Run `seed`, then `reopen` as separate Node processes using the same isolated directory. This Linux Node 24.22.1 proof used an independently owned frozen-lockfile install and an explicit 4,352 MiB build heap on an 8 GiB host; qualify host capacity before copying that build override.

